{"id":4,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"contents":{"kind":"plaintext","value":"encode(value: t, order: byte_order = …) -> [u8]\n\nEncode one fixed-width number into a fresh owned byte array.\nSupports i8/u8, i16/u16, i32/u32, i64/u64 and f32/f64; other types fail compilation.\nPreserves two's-complement and IEEE bits, including signed zero and NaN payloads.\nAllocation failures follow the ordinary Runtime array failure policy.\n\nReturns: Exactly the numeric type's width in bytes, in independent writable storage."},"range":{"end":{"character":29,"line":3},"start":{"character":23,"line":3}}}}Content-Length: 196

